+<main class="subpage-main"><section class="subpage-hero container"><span class="kicker">PLANEBYTE POLICIES</span><h1>Terms of Service</h1><p>Effective 17 November 2026 · planebyte-creem-global-2026-11-17-v3</p></section><section class="container legal-layout"><article class="legal-copy"><section id="terms-0"><h2>1. Who provides the service</h2><p>PlaneByte is the trading/product name used for the service provided by <strong>Planebyte, an individually operated business owned by Piyush Agrawal</strong>, with its legal-notice/business address at <strong>House No. 1005, Attabira, Bargarh, Odisha 768027, India</strong>, referred to as “PlaneByte,” “we,” “us” or “our.” General service enquiries may be sent to contact@planebyte.com. Formal notices may be sent to that address or contact@planebyte.com. Our business website is https://planebyte.com and the service application is https://app.planebyte.com.</p><p>These Terms govern the PlaneByte application and the Intent Radar and Growth Intelligence features made available to your workspace. “You” means the person accepting these Terms and, where that person acts with authority for an organization, that organization. You must be legally able and authorized to enter this agreement. If you act for an organization, you confirm your authority to bind it.</p></section><section id="terms-1"><h2>2. Acceptance and account security</h2><p>Review these Terms and the Privacy Policy before creating an account or purchasing access. We record acceptance of the applicable version. Do not use the service if you cannot accept the applicable agreement.</p><p>New commercial workspace registration requires a company-managed email address. Email/password registration requires verification of mailbox control. Google registration requires a verified Google identity. Existing expressly authorized accounts may continue to use their approved sign-in method. Verification of a mailbox does not establish legal ownership of a company domain or entitle its holder to join every workspace associated with that domain.</p><p>Provide accurate account details, protect passwords and developer credentials, and promptly notify us of suspected compromise. Sessions expire after eight hours and can be revoked. Password reset requires a valid recovery process and revokes existing account sessions. Google-only accounts use Google recovery unless a PlaneByte password has been explicitly configured. Connecting an additional sign-in method requires an authenticated linking process; matching email addresses alone do not authorize an automatic merge.</p></section><section id="terms-2"><h2>3. Workspaces and permitted users</h2><p>Workspace owners manage invitations, membership and roles, subject to purchased seat capacity and server-side permissions. An invitation requires explicit acceptance by its intended recipient. A shared email domain does not automatically create membership or transfer ownership.</p><p>You are responsible for authorized users acting on your behalf, the accuracy and lawful use of information you provide, and the permissions needed to upload or process it. A workspace member&#x27;s personal account and an organization&#x27;s workspace records can have different ownership and retention requirements. Changing employment or removing a member does not by itself authorize deletion of the organization&#x27;s records.</p></section><section id="terms-3"><h2>4. Included service and research limitations</h2><p>The current offering is Intent Radar and Growth Intelligence. Available features and limits are described in the approved plan comparison and your workspace&#x27;s authoritative billing and usage view. Lead Engine is reserved for a future release and is not included in this public offering.</p><p>Research uses sources that are available and authorized for the relevant workflow. Coverage, freshness and results vary by source, geography and query. Public source availability does not override publisher terms or permissions. We do not promise access to every network, an unrestricted crawl, a particular number of prospects or a commercial outcome.</p><p>AI-generated interpretations, scores, profiles, summaries and recommendations may contain errors or omissions. Source quotations and links are evidence to review, not independent verification of a person&#x27;s employment, identity, buying intent or willingness to receive contact. You remain responsible for reviewing results before relying on them. The service does not supply legal, tax, financial or other regulated professional advice.</p><p>Onboarding prepares editable suggestions. Saving a profile or accepting an AI suggestion does not automatically authorize outreach, payment or an unrequested research run. Third-party integrations require their own permissions and may have additional terms. Google sign-in is separate from permission to access a mailbox or other connected service.</p></section><section id="terms-4"><h2>5. New customer setup and three-day card trial</h2><p>New customers must save their company and ideal customer profiles and complete Choose Your Plan &amp; Payment before entering the full Intent Radar dashboard. Setup-only AI capacity is bounded and is not a free product trial. Authentication, saved setup, billing and cancellation remain accessible while product access is restricted.</p><p>A new eligible trial lasts exactly 72 hours from provider-confirmed activation. You must select Starter, Growth or Scale, provide a supported card through secure provider-hosted checkout and explicitly accept recurring authorization. No subscription payment is due during a free trial. The selected plan then renews automatically each month unless canceled. Hosted checkout shows the exact charge amount, currency, first-charge date/time and cancellation terms before authorization. If an unavoidable card-verification charge is required, it must be disclosed and authorized separately; otherwise the advertised free path is unavailable.</p><p>Trial limits are five searches, three AI operations, 150,000 reserved AI tokens, one manual monitor and one user. Scheduled checks, reports, developer API and MCP require paid allowances. One trial is allowed per verified person and business domain; earlier trials count toward eligibility. Failed, canceled or unverified checkout grants no trial or paid access. Existing customer trials and purchased entitlements retain their recorded terms.</p></section><section id="terms-5"><h2>6. Prices, providers and tax</h2><p>Monthly subscription prices are USD59 for Starter, USD149 for Growth and USD379 for Scale. Enterprise is quoted individually. Yearly checkout is disabled until exact prices and allowance timing are approved. Published allowances are subject to their versioned catalog and the verified contract snapshot.</p><p>Eligible international checkout uses Creem, the merchant of record, with tax-inclusive USD product prices. Creem calculates and discloses applicable taxes, payment totals and invoices under its terms. PlaneByte does not store card numbers or CVVs. Creem handles checkout for all supported countries. Changing a country field does not verify billing location or switch an existing provider. PlaneByte has no GSTIN and does not independently add unverified GST.</p><p>Each provider path opens only after merchant permissions, payment acceptance and applicable disclosures are verified. A browser success page is not payment evidence. We activate access only after authenticated provider confirmation and independent reconciliation. Product creation or a webhook test does not establish payment or payout readiness.</p></section><section id="terms-6"><h2>7. Subscription renewal, cancellation and legacy purchases</h2><p>A Creem monthly subscription renews using the provider-confirmed billing period and schedule, rather than an internal timer that charges stored cards. Your selected plan, amount, currency and renewal date are displayed before authorization and in Billing &amp; Subscription. Provider-confirmed failed, unpaid, paused, disputed or expired states can restrict product access while preserving billing and cancellation controls.</p><p>You may cancel future automatic billing through Settings → Billing &amp; Subscription or the secure provider portal without contacting support. Cancellation is complete only when confirmed by the provider. During a trial, cancel before the first-charge date to prevent conversion. Confirmed cancellation preserves access until the agreed current period ends unless mandatory rights, a verified refund or a security restriction require otherwise. We show and email confirmed cancellation; if a request is unverified, we say so and allow status refresh or recovery.</p><p>All new purchases use Creem subscriptions in every supported country, including India where Creem permits transactions. Creem determines available payment methods, local-currency presentation, taxes and invoicing at secure checkout. PlaneByte does not convert USD list prices itself. Existing prepaid purchases preserve their original access dates and consent; they do not silently become recurring subscriptions. No silent provider transfer, early upgrade, proration or unused-time credit is promised. Plan changes with monetary consequences require disclosed amounts, effective dates and explicit authorization.</p></section><section id="terms-7"><h2>8. Allowances and usage</h2><p>Plan allowances, daily safety limits and capacity limits are distinct. The workspace usage view shows the applicable period and remaining capacity. Scheduled checks consume the applicable search and monitor allowances. AI operation counts, reserved token capacity, reported provider tokens and estimated provider cost are separate measurements; an estimate is not a guarantee of actual cost or complete token reporting.</p><p>Limits are enforced on the server. Retries reuse the relevant operation record where supported; an uncertain provider outcome may retain reserved capacity until reconciled. The service can refuse further operations when capacity is exhausted, access expires or a safety limit is reached. Existing saved research is retained according to the approved retention policy. Do not bypass limits, share credentials to evade seat restrictions, or manipulate client state to obtain unpurchased access.</p></section><section id="terms-8"><h2>9. Refunds, billing errors and cancellation</h2><p>For an initial paid purchase, request refund review within seven days of verified payment through Billing or contact@planebyte.com. Include the payment reference and reason without card information. We review duplicate charges, billing errors, service circumstances and applicable rights. No undisclosed usage-percentage exclusion or universal no-refund rule applies. Renewals and other requests are reviewed under their agreement and mandatory rights.</p><p>Canceling a future renewal, leaving checkout, account closure and refunding an already captured payment are separate actions. A free trial has no subscription payment to refund. Refund success and timing are confirmed through the provider; submitting a request does not move money or prove bank settlement. Existing payment and audit records may be retained where legally required.</p></section><section id="terms-9"><h2>10. Customer information and intellectual property</h2><p>You retain your rights in content you provide. You authorize processing of that content to operate the requested service, secure the account, provide support and perform the workflows you authorize, as described in the Privacy Policy. You must have the necessary rights and permissions for that content.</p><p>PlaneByte retains its rights in the service, software and branding. Your access permits use within the purchased or trial scope; it does not transfer ownership of the software. Third-party materials remain subject to their owners&#x27; rights. AI output may not be unique and is not a representation that all underlying material is exclusively owned by you or PlaneByte.</p></section><section id="terms-10"><h2>11. Acceptable use</h2><p>Do not use the service unlawfully, infringe others&#x27; rights, bypass access controls, impersonate another person, attempt unauthorized security testing, extract private content without permission, or interfere with another workspace. Do not use credentials, integrations, sources or developer tools beyond their authorized scope.</p><p>Product access does not authorize cold outreach, mass messaging or disregard of consent, opt-outs and suppression requirements. Features unavailable in your workspace must not be accessed through direct API calls or workers. Report a suspected vulnerability privately to contact@planebyte.com without exposing customer information.</p></section><section id="terms-11"><h2>12. Service operation, suspension and termination</h2><p>We may restrict activity necessary to address account compromise, unlawful use, material misuse, provider restrictions or risks to the service or other users. We will provide an explanation and a route to support when lawful and practicable. A temporary restriction is not authority to erase retained customer or accounting records.</p><p>Service availability depends in part on third-party infrastructure and providers. No uninterrupted service, service-level credit, compliance certification or particular performance commitment is promised unless a separate written agreement expressly supplies one. We may maintain and improve the service; changes affecting paid access are subject to the applicable purchase agreement, approved refund policy and mandatory rights.</p></section><section id="terms-12"><h2>13. Account closure, retention and deletion</h2><p>You may download personal account details and use the available workspace research exports, or request a full export through Sign-in &amp; Security or contact@planebyte.com. Once account closure is verified through the review process, ordinary account data is scheduled for deletion or anonymization within 30 days, subject to the exceptions below. Backups are removed through their normal retention cycle, targeted at no more than 90 days after verified closure. Access expiry alone is not a closure request, and a submitted request does not immediately erase a workspace.</p><p>Submit an authenticated data request in Settings → Account → Sign-in &amp; Security, or contact contact@planebyte.com. The application records a case reference. Support verifies identity, organizational authority, the requested scope and applicable retention exceptions before confirming closure or deletion. Additional information is requested only as needed for a proportionate review. Verified closure starts the tracked retention deadlines; no deletion is claimed until the case has been fulfilled and verified. Contact the same channel with the case reference for status or escalation. Deletion may be limited by applicable legal obligations, payment/refund records, disputes, fraud/security needs, legal holds, and the need to preserve contact history and suppression records. A member&#x27;s deletion request must not automatically remove records controlled by another authorized workspace or erase evidence required to honor an opt-out. We will explain applicable limitations through the approved process.</p></section><section id="terms-13"><h2>14. Responsibilities and mandatory rights</h2><p>Use reasonable care in evaluating source material and AI output, preserving your own necessary records, and managing authorized users. We remain responsible for obligations that applicable law does not permit us to exclude. Nothing in these Terms removes mandatory consumer or data-protection rights, excuses fraud or willful misconduct, or limits liability where such a limitation would be unlawful. No monetary liability cap, indemnity or exclusive foreign court is imposed by these Terms.</p></section><section id="terms-14"><h2>15. Changes, notices and disputes</h2><p>We will identify the published version and effective date of these Terms. Material changes requiring renewed acceptance will be presented through the account or purchase flow before they apply as required by the applicable agreement and law. A revised price does not silently authorize a charge or alter a previously verified order.</p><p>Contact contact@planebyte.com to raise a service or billing concern and provide the relevant workspace/order reference without sending passwords, verification codes or card details. Formal notices use the contracting identity and address in section 1. Applicable mandatory law and lawful rights to seek regulatory or judicial remedies remain available; no unapproved governing-law or venue clause is invented. If a provision cannot lawfully apply, the remaining lawful provisions continue to operate. A separately signed agreement governs only to the extent it expressly varies these Terms for the relevant customer.</p></section><section id="ai-content"><h2>6. AI-generated content &amp; prohibited NSFW outputs</h2><p>PlaneByte's Intent Radar platform includes AI-powered synthesis, summaries, interpretations, and analytical features.</p><p>Users are strictly prohibited from using these features to request, generate, create, or distribute Not Safe for Work (NSFW), pornographic, sexually explicit, or otherwise unlawful sexual content.</p><p>This restriction applies to user prompts, AI-generated interpretations, synthesized reports, summaries, and all other AI-generated outputs.</p><p>Any content involving the sexual exploitation or abuse of minors is strictly prohibited.</p><p>PlaneByte reserves the right to restrict access, remove prohibited content where technically possible, suspend accounts, or terminate services for violations of this policy.</p></section></article></section></main>--- a/src/markup/privacy.html
