-<section id="who"><h2>1. Who is responsible</h2><p>This privacy policy describes how Planebyte Studios ("PlaneByte", "we", "us"), headquartered in Bangalore, India, collects, uses, and safeguards information when you visit planebyte.com, submit an inquiry, book a demo, or interact with our software. Inquiries regarding this policy can be sent to <a href="mailto:contact@planebyte.com">contact@planebyte.com</a>. Effective date: November 2026.</p></section>
-<section id="collection"><h2>2. Information you provide</h2><p>When you submit a contact form or request access, we collect your name, work email address, company name (optional), inquiry topic, and message. When booking a call via Cal.com, you may also provide scheduling preferences and contact information. We request that you never submit confidential passwords, credit card numbers, or private customer records through general inquiry forms.</p><p>We also collect standard technical request headers (such as IP address, browser type, and referrer) strictly for website security, spam prevention, and abuse mitigation via rate-limiting mechanisms.</p></section>
-<section id="uses"><h2>3. How information is used</h2><p>We use your information exclusively to respond to inquiries, arrange product demonstrations, deliver service notices, and provision workspace access. We do not sell your personal information or contact details to third-party data brokers or marketing lists.</p></section>
-<section id="partners"><h2>4. Third-party processors &amp; services</h2><p>We work with trusted infrastructure partners to operate our platform securely:</p><ul><li><b>Hosting:</b> Netlify hosts this marketing website with secure HTTPS and DDoS protection.</li><li><b>Email Delivery:</b> Inquiries submitted through our forms are securely transmitted using Resend to contact@planebyte.com.</li><li><b>Meeting Scheduling:</b> Call booking is powered by Cal.com under its own privacy standards.</li><li><b>Payment Processing:</b> Commercial payment transactions are securely handled by authorized payment gateways (including PayU). PlaneByte never stores payment card credentials.</li></ul></section>
-<section id="retention"><h2>5. Security &amp; data retention</h2><p>We implement industry-standard administrative, technical, and physical safeguards—including encryption in transit (TLS 1.3), access controls, and rate-limiting safeguards—to protect information from unauthorized disclosure. Inquiry records are retained only as long as necessary to fulfill commercial communication or comply with statutory accounting requirements.</p></section>
-<section id="rights"><h2>6. Your rights &amp; choices</h2><p>You have the right to request access to, correction of, or deletion of personal information you have submitted to us. You can exercise these rights at any time by emailing <a href="mailto:contact@planebyte.com">contact@planebyte.com</a>. We respond to verified data requests within 30 days.</p></section>
-<section id="changes"><h2>7. Changes to this policy</h2><p>We review and update this privacy policy periodically to reflect operational, legal, or regulatory changes. Revisions will be published on this page with an updated effective date. Effective date: November 2026.</p></section>
