+<main class="subpage-main"><section class="subpage-hero container"><span class="kicker">PLANEBYTE POLICIES</span><h1>Cancellation Policy & Refund Policy</h1><p>Effective 17 November 2026 · planebyte-creem-global-2026-11-17-v3</p></section><section class="container legal-layout"><article class="legal-copy"><section id="cancellation-0"><h2>Cancel automatic renewal</h2><p>For a provider-confirmed recurring subscription, open Settings → Billing &amp; Subscription and choose Cancel automatic renewal, or use the secure provider billing portal. No support contact is required. Review the confirmed effective date. Cancellation must be confirmed by the provider; a pending or failed request is not shown as successful. Billing and cancellation remain accessible even if product access is restricted.</p><p>For a72-hour card trial, cancel before the displayed first-charge date/time to prevent the selected monthly paid plan from starting. Once cancellation is provider-confirmed, no later automatic charge is authorized by that subscription. Trial or current paid access continues to its agreed end unless mandatory rights, a verified refund or a security restriction require otherwise. A confirmation is shown and sent by transactional email.</p><p>Legacy one-time purchases do not automatically renew and never authorize a recurring card mandate. Their saved start/end dates and original manual-renewal terms remain unchanged.</p></section><section id="cancellation-1"><h2>Canceled or failed checkout</h2><p>If hosted checkout is canceled, fails or remains unverified, your onboarding stays saved at Choose Your Plan &amp; Payment. No trial or paid access is granted. You may reconcile or safely retry the saved checkout. Reaching a success URL does not activate a subscription. Canceling checkout does not refund an independently captured payment; use the refund-review workflow where applicable.</p></section><section id="cancellation-2"><h2>Provider, plan changes and payment failures</h2><p>Creem is the sole provider for all new customer payments. Its hosted checkout applies supported-country, payment-method and compliance restrictions. Those restrictions are not bypassed. Plan changes must disclose the provider amount, effective date, recurring terms and any approved proration before authorization.</p><p>For failed renewal, use Billing &amp; Subscription or the secure provider portal to review payment recovery. Product operations may be restricted while the provider reports unpaid, past-due or expired access; authentication, billing and cancellation remain available. Yearly checkout is unavailable until approved.</p></section><section id="cancellation-3"><h2>Account closure and data</h2><p>You may request account closure, a full export or erasure review through Settings → Account → Sign-in &amp; Security or contact@planebyte.com. The request is recorded and reviewed for identity, workspace authority and retained-record obligations. It does not immediately delete data, remove another user&#x27;s records or issue a refund. Ordinary account data is scheduled for deletion/anonymization within 30 days after verified closure, with backup aging targeted within 90 days, subject to justified exceptions in the Privacy Policy.</p><p>Expiry of access alone preserves saved research under the applicable retention policy. Closure of a personal account and the handling of an organization&#x27;s workspace are separate matters; organizational authority must be verified. Contact support before closure if you need help exporting records or transferring authorized workspace ownership.</p><p>For refund review, use the separate Refund Policy, including its seven-day initial-purchase request window and any additional mandatory rights. For questions or escalation, contact contact@planebyte.com with the order or request reference. No password, OTP or card details are required in that message.</p></section><section id="refund-0"><h2>Initial purchases</h2><p>You may request a refund for an initial prepaid purchase within seven days of verified payment. Submit Request refund review in Settings → Billing &amp; Usage, or email contact@planebyte.com with your order reference and the reason. Do not send passwords, OTPs or card details. The policy applies to the initial purchase; additional rights required by applicable law remain available for every purchase.</p><p>The request is reviewed against the actual purchase, payment evidence, service circumstances and applicable rights. The seven-day window is not an unreviewed promise that every request has already been approved. No undisclosed usage-percentage condition is imposed. If a request cannot be approved in full, we explain the reason and the available support/escalation route. No blanket exclusion of mandatory rights is intended.</p></section><section id="refund-1"><h2>Billing errors, duplicates and uncertain payments</h2><p>Contact us about an incorrect or duplicate charge even if you are unsure whether the initial-purchase window applies. We reconcile the specific transactions before deciding what action is appropriate. A pending payment is not assumed successful. Check your payment history and contact support before paying again when a prior result is uncertain.</p><p>A recorded request is an acknowledgement of review, not proof that money was refunded. Creem processes new financial transactions as merchant of record; historical payments retain their original provider records. A refund is treated as completed only after independent provider verification; actual banking credit timing can vary. We do not promise a settlement deadline that the provider has not confirmed.</p></section><section id="refund-2"><h2>Renewals, subscriptions and legacy fixed terms</h2><p>Canceling a subscription prevents provider-confirmed future renewal; it does not automatically refund a prior charge. Renewal refund requests remain subject to the actual agreement, service circumstances and mandatory rights. Initial paid purchase requests remain eligible for review within seven days. No blanket exclusion of mandatory rights applies.</p><p>Legacy fixed-term purchases retain their original manual-renewal terms. New recurring trials require hosted card authorization and a selected conversion plan; no subscription charge is due during the advertised72hours. Yearly checkout remains disabled. Refunds are processed only through approved provider workflows and are not assumed successful from a browser return.</p></section><section id="refund-3"><h2>Access and retained records</h2><p>A full refund independently confirmed in the original purchase currency revokes the access attributable to that purchase. It does not delete saved research, another purchase or the original accounting record. Partial refunds and missing currency evidence require review; they do not automatically create a new entitlement or a credit balance. Payment/refund and other justified retention exceptions are explained in the Privacy Policy.</p><p>Contact contact@planebyte.com with the case/order reference for status or escalation. Nothing in this policy limits rights that applicable law does not permit us to exclude.</p></section></article></section></main>--- a/src/markup/pricing.html
